<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The planned genocide of the Elvi had not been stopped, but had by necessity re-organised, prioritising the manufacture of deadly micro-organisms. Stocks of viable virus were replenished and the program was back on track within two months. The wounds of the condemned Elvis prisoners had healed and they had regained their resolve. Each were held in isolation, ignorant of the other\'92s fate, but knowing none would ever betray their brothers and sisters. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>In the first isolation chamber Elvis was strapped to an interrogation chair, gagged and blindfolded. Electrodes and a tangle of wires attached him to a jumble of medical devices and machines haphazardly assembled around him. His breathing remained slow and regular, the heart monitor beeped, sounding out the cadence of dignified calm. The gaping sore that had taken the place of his ear had been proficiently tended to and was healing, albeit slowly. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93We are going to test a viral agent on you Mr Elvis. It is expected that you will die.\'94 Dr\'85\'85 said with a smile. \'93I am going to take off your blindfold and gag. Please don\'92t yell or scream. It will do you no good and only serve to annoy.\'94 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I have no reason to scream\'94 Elvis said. \'93You do not frighten me. You do not frighten any of us. Libera Elvi Superbia! \'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93What is that supposed to mean?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Deliver Elvi Freedom!\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93No, I think you guys should brush up on you Latin.\'94 Dr ???? corrected. \'93I will be injecting the viral agent and the effects should be immediate.\'94 The doctor approached with an old-style syringe and needle and making no attempt to locate a blood vessel, plunged it into subcutaneous tissue of the neck and forcefully pressed the plunger.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The pain was instantaneous and excruciating, but the Elvis did not blink or even contort his face, but the heart monitor began beeping faster and faster and yet faster again. His breathing became laboured and he coughed violently as his organs began to bleed out. In less that five minutes the Elvis was dead, drowned in his own fluids, blood and snot foaming from nose and mouth.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Well that was successful, but injection is a very inefficient delivery system.\'94 Dr >??? Said to his colleagues. \'93We will have to weaponise the agent. Atomised liquid or powder?\'94 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Atomising the virus should be quicker, but less efficient than concentrated airborne powder.\'94 Dr>>>> replied. \'93I can work on the liquid version of the agent and you can get onto reducing it to powder.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93We are yet to work out the dosage. Clearly we gave our subject far more that actually needed to ensure death. Let\'92s write this up and get onto the final phase of development.\'94 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Keep the body on ice. Director Hardman wants to send the Elvi a message.\'94 \
